In case titled, State of Himachal Pradesh v. Umed Ram Sharma (1986) 2 SCC 68, Hon'ble Apex Court has held that entire State .
of Himachal Pradesh is a hilly area and without workable roads, no communication is possible;
every person is entitled to life as enjoined in Article 21 of the Constitution of India; every person has right under Article 19 (1) (b) of the Constitution of India to move freely, throughout of the territory of India; for the residents of hilly areas, access to road is access to life itself.
